{"id":56760,"ord":120,"n_segments":179,"prev":56759,"next":56761,"doc":{"id":"68154","title":"68154_Gus Johnson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Gus Johnson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68154/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68154"},"chapter":"Postwar: Chicago, Vinson, Hines and Cootie","title":"Cootie Williams's small band at the Savoy: personnel","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"After Hines broke up he played at the Savoy with Cootie's small band, with Bob Miller, Leonard Swain and Rupert Cole.","period":"1948","year_from":1948,"year_to":1948,"words":248,"start":[248,1],"end":[249,19],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68154#s56760","tags":{"places":[{"name":"New York","focus":0,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Savoy Ballroom","focus":1,"city":"New York"}],"bands":[{"name":"Cootie Williams' small band","focus":1,"leader":"Cootie Williams"},{"name":"Jay McShann Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Jay McShann"},{"name":"Earl Hines Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Earl Hines"}]},"people":[{"name":"Arnold Jarvis","qid":null,"n":4},{"name":"Bob Merrill","qid":"Q42175666","n":4},{"name":"Cootie Williams","qid":"Q523899","n":3},{"name":"Jay McShann","qid":"Q1684347","n":2},{"name":"Eddie Vinson","qid":"Q1283017","n":1},{"name":"Leonard Swain","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Rupert Cole","qid":"Q64738149","n":1}],"story":{"theme":18,"theme_name":"Getting paid: wages, tips and leaving over money","community":39,"community_name":"Battling at the Savoy Ballroom","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":248,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"I follow you, I'm sorry, you're right. Now, this, which may not even be right, says that you worked with Cootie Williams -- probably what they're --"},{"p":248,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Well, I worked with Cootie Williams' small band."},{"p":248,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, did you?"},{"p":248,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oh, yes."},{"p":248,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"At the Savoy?"},{"p":248,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"At the Savoy, yeah."},{"p":248,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"After Cootie broke up the big band."},{"p":248,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"After he broke up the big band, I --"},{"p":248,"b":9,"s":"MS.","x":"Well, who else was in that?"},{"p":248,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Um, --"},{"p":248,"b":11,"s":"MS.","x":"Was the other trumpet player -- Merrell?"},{"p":248,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Bob Miller?"},{"p":248,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":248,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Bob Miller, he was in the band. See, Bob Miller used to be with McShann."},{"p":248,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, yeah."},{"p":248,"b":16,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"See, he used to be in McShann's band."},{"p":248,"b":17,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":248,"b":18,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"He was with McShann when we came to New York."},{"p":248,"b":19,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":249,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Leonard Swain was playing bass."},{"p":249,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh?"},{"p":249,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Myself, --"},{"p":249,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Who was playing piano?"},{"p":249,"b":4,"s":"","x":"(Arnold Jarvis--ed.)"},{"p":249,"b":5,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Jarvis."},{"p":249,"b":6,"s":"MS.","x":"I don't know him."},{"p":249,"b":7,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"He's from New York."},{"p":249,"b":8,"s":"MS.","x":"Alto?"},{"p":249,"b":9,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"No, piano."},{"p":249,"b":10,"s":"MS.","x":"Don't know him. What's his --"},{"p":249,"b":11,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Jarvis -- oh, what is it, now? I can't think --"},{"p":249,"b":12,"s":"MS.","x":"I'm putting you on the spot. But it's very hard to put a name to everybody you know."},{"p":249,"b":13,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Well, I know his first name was Jarvis."},{"p":249,"b":14,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah, well, that's all right. If I need to find out, I can find out."},{"p":249,"b":15,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And we had an alto player. I saw his picture in here somewhere. The name, too. (Rupert Cole--ed.)"},{"p":249,"b":16,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh. He was, like, taking Cleanhead's place, huh?"},{"p":249,"b":17,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yeah, just in playing, yeah. He didn't sing. Because Bob Merrill was doing the singing."},{"p":249,"b":18,"s":"MS.","x":"Yes, that's right."},{"p":249,"b":19,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"See."}]}